# Little Harness: optional configuration for teaching and HotpotQA worker CLIs.
# Start with LEARN.md: Labs 0-4 run offline without loading this file or .env.
# Completed preview: python3 -m lessons.preview
# Then build the loop: python3 -m lessons.lab00_basics --check --stage 1
# Lab limits are set in lesson code/options, not by these environment variables.
# No new settings or credentials are needed for the labs.
# If .env exists, edit it deliberately; do not overwrite it with this template.
# Otherwise copy to .env as needed. Application CLIs load it from the current directory.
# Existing shell variables take priority (unset them to use the file's values).
# Supports KEY=value, quotes, comments and optional export; no shell/variable expansion.

# Provider: anthropic (default), openai, openai-chat or gateway (Grove's AI Gateway)
# gateway picks the route from HARNESS_MODEL: claude-* -> /anthropic/v1, anything else -> /openai/v1
# (gateway-anthropic and gateway-openai force a route)
# HARNESS_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Provider keys are for live model calls; offline labs and scripted demos do not need them.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Model ID (default: claude-sonnet-5-5 for anthropic, gpt-5.6-sol for gateway; required for openai/openai-chat)
HARNESS_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# Optional: override the base URL (proxy or local server, e.g. http://localhost:11434/v1); the key becomes optional
# HARNESS_BASE_URL=

# Optional: name of the variable that holds the key, if it is not the provider default
# HARNESS_API_KEY_ENV=AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY

# Optional, anthropic only: if your key is not scoped to a single workspace
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=wrkspc_...

# Optional: history size (JSON characters) that triggers compaction (default: 40000)
# HARNESS_COMPACT_CHARS=40000

# Optional: per-task limits for the teaching CLI (unset leaves limits disabled).
# Logical model calls include compaction; tool attempts include invalid/denied requests.
# HARNESS_MAX_MODEL_CALLS=12
# HARNESS_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=12
# HARNESS_MAX_TOKENS=12000
# HARNESS_MAX_SECONDS=60
# Time/tokens are checked between operations, not hard limits on running calls.
# Token limits require provider usage; scripted demos do not report usage.

# Optional: run tools in disposable processes with a positive per-tool timeout.
# HARNESS_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5
# Per-tool decorator timeouts override this default; the remaining task deadline can shorten it.
# Requires importable module-level functions; parent-memory changes do not propagate.
# Timeout/crash stops the task without retrying; writes may already have happened.
# Process isolation is not a security sandbox and does not time out approval/model calls.

# Optional: durable action metadata and conservative crash/restart recovery guards.
# HARNESS_JOURNAL=execution.sqlite3
# Must be outside HARNESS_WORKSPACE, separate from trace/session, in an existing directory.
# Uncertain actions or unclosed runs block further work until human-verified recovery.
# Inspect with: python3 -m harness inspect execution.sqlite3 --pending
# No arguments/outputs are stored, and no tool actions are automatically replayed.

# Optional: allow only tools explicitly declared read-only (unset/0 preserves defaults).
# HARNESS_READ_ONLY=1
# Blocks write_file, http_get and unclassified tools before approval/journal/worker startup.
# Application-level dispatch only, not an OS sandbox or protection against data disclosure.
# Library callers pass ToolPolicy explicitly; HotpotQA workers do not inherit this flag.

# Optional: teaching JSONL traces are metadata-only by default. Opt in deliberately:
# HARNESS_TRACE_CONTENT=1
# Content traces include tasks, model/tool content, summaries and error details.
# Event content is controlled separately. Sessions/console/results may still contain content.
# HotpotQA evaluation explicitly uses full benchmark traces; this setting does not change it.
# examples.support_agent never loads .env; use --trace-content for that example only.

# Optional: interactive mode saves the conversation here and resumes it (default: session.json)
# HARNESS_SESSION=session.json

# Optional: sandbox directory for the file tools (default: ./workspace)
# HARNESS_WORKSPACE=workspace

# Optional: curated read-only corpus outside the workspace (default: ./knowledge)
# Only top-level .md/.txt documents are searched. Never put credentials here.
# HARNESS_KNOWLEDGE=knowledge
# For the bundled ten-question HotpotQA lesson instead:
# HARNESS_KNOWLEDGE=datasets/hotpotqa/knowledge
